                "text": "**Examining Color Frames**\n\nOkay, I'm now focused on these color frames. Each has a colored boundary and an interior dot. The task involves these shapes with openings. I'm taking a closer look at a box.\n\n\n**Analyzing Leakage Behavior**\n\nI've been examining how these colored dots \"leak\" out of the boxes through the openings. It seems the dot's color floods the interior and then forms a line outside the box, across the whole width if the opening is on the top or bottom of a box, and filling from top to bottom if the opening is on the left or right. I'm noting the pattern in the output related to the position of the openings. It is important to note that the shape extent is critical to determine the \"leakage\" area.\n\n\n**Defining Leakage Rules**\n\nI see a clear pattern emerging: the interior fills with the dot color. I confirmed that the color data at the dot's location completely fills the interior. The opening then determines the \"leakage\" behavior. Now, I have to figure out the exact rule governing where the \"leaked\" color appears outside the box. It spans the width or height, depending on the opening's location, matching the color! I'm now testing two boxes, and trying to solidify a robust rule to describe the effect.\n\n\n",
